{
 "duration": 42.632,
 "voice": "am_michael",
 "speed": 1.05,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "A man once walked into a room and bought an entire airport.",
   "start": 0.3,
   "end": 3.726
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "For one dollar.",
   "start": 3.886,
   "end": 4.827
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "No, seriously.",
   "start": 4.987,
   "end": 5.972
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "See, in 2014, a British airport called Manston went bankrupt.",
   "start": 6.132,
   "end": 10.999
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "Runways, terminals, hangars \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the whole thing.",
   "start": 11.159,
   "end": 15.245
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "The owners tried to sell it.",
   "start": 15.405,
   "end": 16.756
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Nobody wanted it.",
   "start": 16.916,
   "end": 18.018
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "It sat there, empty, with planes going quiet one by one.",
   "start": 18.178,
   "end": 21.653
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "Then a millionaire named Charlie Sherwood showed up.",
   "start": 21.813,
   "end": 24.34
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "And said: I'll take it.",
   "start": 24.5,
   "end": 25.746
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "For one pound.",
   "start": 25.906,
   "end": 26.899
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "That's about a dollar.",
   "start": 27.059,
   "end": 28.143
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "The owners said yes.",
   "start": 28.303,
   "end": 29.484
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "So he signed the papers, handed over a single coin,",
   "start": 29.644,
   "end": 32.964
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "and walked out the owner of a full-sized international airport.",
   "start": 33.324,
   "end": 36.709
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "text": "Because sometimes the best deal in history costs less than a candy bar.",
   "start": 36.869,
   "end": 41.232
  }
 ]
}